WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:03.736
-We'd like to begin tonight

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:05.204
by saying a few words

00:00:05.204 --> 00:00:09.041
about the horrific mass
shootings in Dayton and El Paso.

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:11.777
This was a heartbreaking weekend
of unspeakable tragedy

00:00:11.777 --> 00:00:15.281
and, yet, one that disturbingly
feels all too familiar.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:18.485
Of course, as we all know
by now, there's an epidemic

00:00:18.485 --> 00:00:20.754
of gun violence and mass
shootings in this country

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:23.856
and, no matter how difficult,
we cannot become numb to it,

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:26.126
but it's also not just
about guns.

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:27.560
The shooting in El Paso was

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.296
an act of white supremacist
domestic terrorism

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.965
specifically targeting
Hispanics.

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.800
It's a threat that is
growing and real.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.068
These are facts we must look
squarely in the eye,

00:00:36.068 --> 00:00:37.703
no matter how monstrous.

00:00:37.703 --> 00:00:40.707
The spread of violent white
supremacy has been fueled

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.441
by racist vitriol;

00:00:42.441 --> 00:00:44.377
warning of invasions
by immigrants,

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.012
language that is
frequently echoed

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:48.614
by right-wing media outlets
and, of course, the president;

00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:50.683
and, on top of that,
there is, of course,

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:53.519
too much easy access to weapons
of war that should be outlawed.

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:55.588
This is a moment that demands
moral clarity

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.590
and urgency from our
political leaders

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:01.561
and so, now that we're seeing
the political world react,

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.162
we thought we might
at least try to offer

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:04.730
a few thoughts
on what's happening.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:07.233
For more on this, it's time for
"A Closer Look."

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:10.102 line:0%
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]
[ Cheer and applause ]

00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:12.305
[ Applause continues ]

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:15.708
As of Sunday, we've had 251
mass shootings in this country,

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.009
in just 216 days.

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:19.112
And, first, let's just make
clear, right off the bat,

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:21.147
that we know there is
a clear correlation

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:22.915
between the number of guns
we have in this country

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:25.819
and the number of gun-related
deaths we have in this country.

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:29.355
For one thing, America has 4.4%
of the world's population,

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:32.125
but almost half
of its civilian-owned guns.

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.226
I mean, just look at this chart
from the website Vox,

00:01:34.226 --> 00:01:36.095
comparing gun ownership
to gun-related deaths.

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:38.998
Here are a bunch of other
developed countries

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:40.332
and here's where we are.

00:01:40.332 --> 00:01:42.701
We're farther away
from the UK on this chart

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:44.437
than we are in real life.

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:46.406
[ Laughter ]
There are proven,

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:48.074
straightforward,
widely popular ways

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:49.475
that we can at least begin
to address

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:51.877
this epidemic of gun violence
and then, of course,

00:01:51.877 --> 00:01:53.913
there's the issue
of the president's racist,

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.081
anti-immigrant rhetoric

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.983
and the growing threat
of white supremacy.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.751
Our political leaders
should have to answer

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:01.687
for where they stand on these
issues, and, yet, at first,

00:02:01.687 --> 00:02:04.056
some senior Republicans
refused to even go on TV

00:02:04.056 --> 00:02:05.124
and answer questions about it,

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:07.126
as CNN's Jake Tapper noted

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:08.728
on his show on Sunday morning.

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:10.129
-We're gonna talk
with at least four

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:13.232
presidential candidates today
about what they would do

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:16.936
to stop this epidemic
of mass shootings and shootings.

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:19.972
We should note that we invited
the Republican governor,

00:02:19.972 --> 00:02:22.508
lieutenant governor, and both
Republican U.S. senators

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:25.611
representing Texas
to join us this morning.

00:02:25.611 --> 00:02:26.845
They all declined.

00:02:26.845 --> 00:02:30.016
The Republican governor
of Ohio also declined.

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:32.886
We also asked the White House
to provide someone

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:34.954
to discuss these shootings.

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:37.723
That request, too, was declined.

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:39.858
-So, basically, we tried to get
the Republican governor

00:02:39.858 --> 00:02:42.161
and lieutenant governor,
senior senator, junior senator,

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:43.963
the Republican dogcatcher,
the Republican

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:45.264
[ Laughter ]
sanitation commissioner.

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:46.999
We even tried to get
the Republican elephant,

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:48.367
but it literally ran away.

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:50.369
[ Laughter fading ]
[ Zap! ]

00:02:50.369 --> 00:02:51.871
Let me just say,
as a general rule,

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:54.940
when you're spending all
of your time dodging questions

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.308
from journalists and reporters,

00:02:56.308 --> 00:02:58.811
that usually means you're
on the wrong side of history.

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:01.247
It's like when the president
tweeted his racist attacks

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:03.049
on four Democratic
congresswomen of color,

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:06.953
Republicans literally ran into
elevators to avoid reporters.

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:09.555
-He said that these
progressive congresswomen

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:12.591
should go back
to their countries.

00:03:12.591 --> 00:03:15.161
I'm wondering what your
reaction is to that.

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:19.365
-I'm working hard as I can
on reducing

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.200
healthcare costs.
[ Elevator chimes ]

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.302
I'm not giving
a daily commentary

00:03:23.302 --> 00:03:25.304
on the president's tweets.
-But these are, you know,

00:03:25.304 --> 00:03:27.373
racist tweets.

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.642
Do you have any concerns
about it?

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:35.181
-The president said that
these minority congresswomen

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:36.182
should go back
to their countries.

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:37.350
Do you have a response?

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.952
-I hadn't read that,
but I'll go check it out.

00:03:39.952 --> 00:03:41.421
[ Laughter ]
Man, at this point,

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:43.122
if reporters want an answer,
they're going to have to start

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.391
dressing up
as elevator operators.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.160
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.362
And then, when Republicans
finally did speak up,

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:51.464
they acted as if the reasons
for these attacks

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:53.866
were somehow mysterious,
even though we know the facts

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.234
about the epidemic of gun deaths

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:56.703
and mass shootings
in this country

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.003
and we know that the threat

00:03:58.003 --> 00:04:00.205
